.TH SHUCK 1 "August 2026" "shuck 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shuck \- get the documents out of a JavaScript shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shuck
.I url
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shuck
renders a page in headless Chrome, clicks open every tab, accordion and
.B <details>
element it can find, and then prints or downloads the documents behind them.
.PP
It exists for document registers that reveal their file lists only after user
interaction, where
.BR curl (1),
.BR wget (1)
and even
.B chrome --dump-dom
see an empty page.
.PP
By default only links that look like documents are listed \(em those with a file
extension, or a URL containing
.BR download ,
.BR attachment ,
.B getContent
and similar. Names are taken from the anchor text, or, when that text is
uninformative ("View", "Download"), from the nearest ancestor carrying real words.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-match " STR"
Keep only links whose name or URL contains
.IR STR ,
case-insensitively.
.TP
.B \-\-all
List every link, not just document-looking ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-get " DIR"
Download the matched links into
.IR DIR ,
naming each file from its label.
.TP
.BI \-\-click " SEL|TEXT"
Click a CSS selector, or the smallest element containing
.IR TEXT .
Repeatable; runs before the automatic expansion.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-expand
Do not automatically open tabs, accordions and
.BR <details> .
.TP
.BI \-\-dom " FILE"
Write the rendered DOM to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit results as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait " SEC"
Settle time after load and after each interaction. Default 3.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress progress output on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHUCK_CHROME
Path to the Chrome, Chromium, Brave or Edge binary, if it is not in a standard
location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on usage error, 130 if interrupted.
.SH CAVEATS
.B shuck
clicks things. Do not point it at a page with destructive controls without
.B \-\-no\-expand
and an explicit
.BR \-\-click .
It cannot get past logins, paywalls or CAPTCHAs and does not try.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR wget (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jonathan O'Brien
